The rust png codec cannot be built for Android out of the box. Two lists in
MODULE.bazel leave out aarch64-linux-android:

- rust.toolchain extra_target_triples: no Rust standard library for the target.
- crate.from_specs supported_platform_triples: crate_universe marks every crate
  (cxx first) incompatible with //bazel/platform:android_arm64, and analysis
  stops with "Target //rust/png:ffi_rs is incompatible".

cargo_bindeps is left alone. cxxbridge-cmd runs on the exec platform (linux
x86_64), not on the target.

MODULE.bazel.lock is part of this patch on purpose. Changing the crate
extension's inputs invalidates its locked result, and Bazel then resolves the
unpinned transitive crates again, at whatever crates.io serves that day. The
lock below is the one that resolution produced on 2026-10-02 (161 crate repos,
newer patch releases than upstream's lock, e.g. cc 1.4.4 -> 1.5.1). Shipping
it keeps Android rebuilds on the same crates. Only the crate extension's
entry differs from upstream's lock.

Windows does not take this patch, so it keeps upstream's lock and crates.

Checked on Skia 152 (0873ec164a) under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04:
  bazelisk build //rust/png:ffi_rs --platforms=//bazel/platform:android_arm64
gives libffi_rs.a whose 960 objects are all ELF64 AArch64, and the resulting
Skia runs on an arm64 device.

